      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The main argument for originalism is that the Constitution should be interpreted based on the public understanding of its text at the time it was ratified. Proponents believe this approach limits judicial bias and respects the will of the framers and the public in the 18th and 19th centuries. This perspective argues that the Constitution is a fixed, authoritative document, not a source for the judge to create new policy.",
