    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i've also heard people say it's kind of just a way for judges to push their own political agendas under the guise of law. how do scholars who disagree with originalism usually frame their critiques?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Skeptics argue that \"original intent\" is often impossible to definitively determine, as the political context of the time is inherently biased. They claim that an overly rigid focus on the past can make the Constitution unworkable in a rapidly changing, modern society.\n\nThese critics often champion \"living constitutionalism,\" which posits that the Constitution must evolve to address contemporary social and moral issues to maintain its relevance and justice.",
      "source": "target",
